      "content": "The consensus among many urban planners is that continuous highway expansion often leads to induced demand, meaning new roads quickly fill up with more cars, defeating the purpose. While road maintenance is necessary, the strategic long-term argument for mass transit centers on systemic efficiency versus simply accommodating more vehicles. Therefore, many experts view significant new highway construction as a temporary palliative measure rather than a sustainable, forward-looking solution for growing urban populations.",
